    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d426-a1-a1-a9">

                <pb facs="0752" n="682" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg682"/>

                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Luis Potosi,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 30, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I received your communication of yesterday,
                    saying that the Archduke Ferdinand Maximilian, of Hapsburg, expressed the desire
                    before his death that his mortal remains be intrusted to you and Dr. Samuel
                    Basch, to be transported to Europe.</p>
                <p>As I have already informed you, the government of the republic, for good and
                    sufficient reasons, cannot allow the body of the archduke to be carried to
                    Europe. Therefore I regret to say to you that the government cannot issue the
                    orders you request for that purpose.</p>
                <p>I take the occasion to repeat to you, Baron, that I am your very obedient and
                    respectful servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. LERDO DE TEJADA.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Baron <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. V. Magnus</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
